“Good morning everyone! Before we jump into the presentation, I thought we’d start with something fun and interactive to wake everyone up a little.” 😄

“So, quick audience participation — no pressure, but I want everyone involved.”

“How would you rate your gardening experience?”

“Let’s see — who here is a Green Thumb Pro? The people who can grow anything and somehow every plant survives?”

(Pause and react to people raising hands)

“Nice! We may need gardening tips from you after this meeting.”

“What about our Growing Learners — you’ve tried a few things, maybe kept a plant alive for at least a month?”

(Pause for laughs)

“Any Total Beginners? Be honest! No judgment here — some of us struggle to keep even a tiny plant alive.”

(Laugh lightly)

“And finally… who’s just here for lunch and enjoying the gardens?”

(People will laugh)

“Honestly, whichever category you fall into, that’s completely okay.”

“Because this is really what community is about — learning together, trying something new, connecting with others, and just taking a break from our normal day-to-day work.”

“And fun fact — apparently spending time in gardens can reduce stress, so technically we’re investing in wellness too!”

“Speaking of community and connection, that’s actually a perfect transition into what CAPSA is all about and why we do what we do.”

⸻

“At CAPSA, our mission is really about creating an inclusive and supportive space for Asian American and Pacific Islander associates.”

“But more than that, it’s about building connections, creating opportunities for growth, celebrating culture, and supporting one another — both personally and professionally.”

“We want this to be a place where people feel welcomed, heard, and empowered.”

“And the exciting part is — this community grows because of people like all of you.”

“We currently have open positions within CAPSA, so if you’ve ever wanted to get more involved, contribute ideas, or make an impact — this is a great opportunity.”

“Please feel free to reach out to Velshey if you’re interested in joining.”

“And if you’re curious but want to learn more first, I highly encourage everyone to join the ARG meeting happening next month.”

“It’s a great way to meet people, understand what we do, and see where you might want to get involved.”

“At the end of the day, CAPSA is about community — and the more voices and participation we have, the stronger we become together.”

“Hopefully we’ll see some new faces joining us soon. Thank you everyone!”
